    pass 2 (L2 likelihood tiers): constants, BigQuery views + gold MERGE, adapter columns, lab notebook, tests
    
    Second classification layer: every open deal of every pipeline binned by the certainty its pipeline records — icalps_oppocertainty
    for Icalps (number, 799/800 filled), hs_deal_stage_probability elsewhere — into Tier4_pipeline (< 0.5), Tier3 (≥ 0.5), Tier2 (≥ 0.75),
    Tier1 (≥ 0.9); closed deals Closed_won / Closed_lost. Both properties are fractions, so the operator's 50/75/90 % are 0.5/0.75/0.9.
    
    - scoring/deal_tiers_v1.constants.json: edges, labels, closed labels, certainty source per pipeline, watch properties and webhook
      events for the event lane, the deal_tier_v1 property definition (enumeration, group dealinformation), the unusable properties.
    - sql/deal_tiers_v1.sql: deal_certainty_v1 → deal_tiers_v1 (RANGE_BUCKET(certainty, [0.5, 0.75, 0.9]) ≡ numpy.digitize; an unknown
      closed state is never tiered) → deal_tiers (gold, retired_at) + deal_tiers_history + deal_tiers_summary_v1.
    - sql/deal_tiers_apply.sql: the scheduled MERGE keyed on @run_time: 36 h freshness guard and half-rows guard, one source row per deal,
      IS DISTINCT FROM → previous_tier/last_changed_at, unchanged rows touch computed_at only, never-tiered deals not inserted,
      WHEN NOT MATCHED BY SOURCE retires deals gone from the sync, history rows for this run's changes and retirements only.
    - sql/deals_synced_v1.sql exposes icalps_oppocertainty, is_closed, is_closed_won; sql/apply.sh applies the tier views last.
    - notebooks/l2_deal_tiers.ipynb (lane N, the lab): snapshot through main.HubSpot with every stage's hs_v2_date_entered_<id>, fill
      rates, distributions, numpy.digitize tiers, calibration by stage entry against each stage's configured probability, deal_tiers_lab
      and a per-deal RANGE_BUCKET == digitize proof, equality with the gold table, the property definition and StackSync mapping rows.
    - tests/test_deal_tiers.py (constants ↔ SQL ↔ bisect reference, MERGE clauses and guards); tests/test_notebook.py covers every notebook.
    - .claude/skills/pass-sequence/scripts/build_surfaces_xlsx.py accepts any three surface ids (pass-1 workbook byte-identical).
    
    Reviewed adversarially before commit (fixed: retirement of cleared/deleted deals, non-existent property group, functions-framework not
    installed in the kernel, calibration against the entrants' current probability instead of the stage's, NULL-skipping comparisons).
    
